From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: queue: eight requests in the queue

The queue depth of 64 gives each request a scatterlist of max_segs
entries: 4 KiB with the 256 descriptors of dw_mmc, 256 KiB in all for a
card that takes one request at a time.  Eight requests queue 1 MiB of
I/O, more than the card has in flight.  On a machine with 16 MiB, the
difference is 1.5 % of the RAM.
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c b/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@
 }
 
 /* Set queue depth to get a reasonable value for q->nr_requests */
-#define MMC_QUEUE_DEPTH 64
+#define MMC_QUEUE_DEPTH 8
 
 /**
  * mmc_init_queue - initialise a queue structure.
